Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: avoid hard rfkill on the Surface Laptop 7

Port the Surface Laptop 7 rfkill workaround to Ubuntu linux 7.2.0-5.5.
The WCN7850 initializes successfully on the Romulus boards but reports a
persistent hardware block after firmware rfkill configuration. Seen on
the 15-inch, and on the 13.8-inch (X1P64100) at its first Linux boot:
the adapter is listed but cannot be switched on.

Skip that configuration only for WCN7850 hw2.0 on microsoft,romulus15
and microsoft,romulus13 (both 13.8-inch trees carry that compatible).
Keep the existing capability and ACPI checks and preserve normal rfkill
handling on other boards. No public data structures or exports change.

Based on the community workaround:
https://github.com/bryce-hoehn/linux-surface-laptop-7/blob/main/patches/0001-wifi-rfkill-hack.patch

This is a local workaround pending a proper platform rfkill fix.
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -80,6 +80,14 @@
 	if (ath12k_acpi_get_disable_rfkill(ab))
 		return 0;

+	/* Avoid the persistent hard block after rfkill setup on these boards. */
+	if (ab->hw_rev == ATH12K_HW_WCN7850_HW20 &&
+	    (of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,romulus15") ||
+	     of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,romulus13"))) {
+		ath12k_info(ab, "applying Surface Laptop 7 rfkill workaround\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	for (i = 0; i < ab->num_radios; i++) {
 		ar = ab->pdevs[i].ar;

